  "text": "Priya (Design): quick pass on the header a11y \u2014 several folks flagged odd tab jumps in the dark theme this morning.\nOmar (Frontend): yep, reproduces in Safari+VO and on Win+NVDA sporadically. tab seems to skip the search input and land on the bell.\nLuca (QA): repro steps i used: macOS 12 + Safari 16 + VoiceOver. load dashboard > tab across top > after project picker -> hits help icon then notifications, never reaches search.\nNaomi (A11y): that pattern usually means a hidden focusable or DOM order mismatch. can we get the header markup?\nOmar (Frontend): here's the simplified header DOM: ```html\n<header class=\"app-header\">\n  <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\">Redwood</a>\n  <div class=\"proj-switch\" tabindex=\"0\">Team A</div>\n  <button class=\"icon-btn help\" aria-hidden=\"false\">? <span class=\"sr-only\">Help center</span></button>\n  <input id=\"global-search\" placeholder=\"Search\">\n  <button class=\"icon-btn notif\" aria-label=\"Notifications\"></button>\n</header>\n```\nNaomi (A11y): two quick things: 1) the `tabindex=0` on non-semantic divs can cause order oddities; replace with `<button>` or `role=\"button\"` + keyboard handlers. 2) check any offscreen skip links or injected anchors \u2014 browsers sometimes prioritize them differently.\nPriya (Design): we do have a skip link that becomes visible on focus: `<a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>` \u2014 intended for keyboard users. is that problematic?\nLuca (QA): in my run the skip-link was focusable immediately even though visually offscreen, and VoiceOver read it before the brand. that reorders everything.\nNaomi (A11y): common. The pattern is to keep skip link first in DOM but only inject it visually when a keyboard interaction is detected; another technique is to set it to not be focusable unless 'keyboard mode' is active (`.skip-link{position: absolute; left: -9999px;} .keyboard-mode .skip-link{left:0; top:0;}`) or toggle `tabindex` from -1 -> 0.\nOmar (Frontend): toggling tabindex sounds safest. we'll set `tabindex=-1` then switch to 0 via JS on first Tab key.\nPriya (Design): separate but related: contrast in dark theme \u2014 the thin divider under header is almost invisible (we used #2c2f33 on #0b0c0e). Naomi measured it and it fails contrast.\nNaomi (A11y): correct \u2014 ratio is ~2.5:1. For small/semi-bold text we need 4.5:1. Options: darken the divider to #3e4146 or use a subtle glow. Also ensure focus rings meet contrast (outline color + background).\nOmar (Frontend): for focus, propose using the brand accent `#7bd389` as a 3px outline with offset; it hits contrast and feels consistent. sample CSS: ```css\n:focus { outline: 3px solid #7bd389; outline-offset: 2px; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(123,211,137,0.14); }\n```\nPriya (Design): nice \u2014 that matches our palette. another nit: icon buttons with counts (notif) include `span.sr-only` text like \"0 new\" inside the button which gets read out even when it's decorative. can we handle counts differently?\nNaomi (A11y): avoid mixing sr-only live text inside controls. Better pattern: keep button label generic (`aria-label=\"Notifications\"`) and update a separate `aria-live` region when counts change. If you must announce count on focus, compute `aria-label` dynamically when count > 0.\nLuca (QA): i'll test both approaches. also noticed the search placeholder is just \"Search\" \u2014 let's make it more descriptive for screen reader users.\nPriya (Design): agreed. change to \"Search projects and models\" per earlier briefs.\nOmar (Frontend): noted. i'll also remove explicit `tabindex` from the project switcher and ensure keyboard handlers (enter/space) exist on it. adding `role=\"button\"` and making it focusable only via semantic button is better.\nNaomi (A11y): checklist for PR please: 1) ensure skip-link tabindex toggles with keyboard-mode, 2) replace div-with-tabindex with semantic button or role + correct keyboard handlers, 3) ensure icon-only buttons have concise `aria-label`s, 4) move live count updates to `aria-live` region, 5) dark theme divider >= 4.5:1 for body text, 6) focus styles use visible high-contrast outline.\nOmar (Frontend): will include NVDA/VO test notes and a short screen recording. also adding unit test for keyboard-mode toggling.\nLuca (QA): i'll run cross-browser a11y smoke: mac/vo, win/nvda, chromevox, ios/vox. will post any failures.\nci-bot: a11y-linter queued for run #1580 by Omar.\nPriya (Design): thanks all. i'll update the figma with darker divider and a clear focus token, and link the PR when ready. :sparkles:\nNaomi (A11y): appreciate it. small copy suggestion \u2014 add `aria-describedby` on search if we keep contextual tips, e.g., \"Press / to focus search\".\nOmar (Frontend): good call, adding `aria-describedby` and a small helper visually hidden but available to screen readers.\nPriya (Design): OK shipping plan: frontend PR with changes -> QA sweep -> a11y signoff. target EOD Thursday.\nLuca (QA): noted. i'll prioritize the sweep once PR is up.\nPriya (Design): closing this thread when PR merged. thanks team! :white_check_mark:"
}